---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/base-layout.astro';
import ReportViewer from '../components/report-viewer.astro';
import CommandPalette from '../components/command-palette.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sample report"
  description="A complete sample penetration test report from Attestor Security, produced against OWASP Juice Shop. Read it in full in the browser, or download the PDF."
  path="/sample-report"
  ogImage="/og/sample-report.png"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Sample</p>
      <h1>Read the report before you buy the engagement</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the full document you would receive, with nothing removed. We produced it against
        OWASP Juice Shop, an application built to be insecure, so there is no client data to redact
        and you can reproduce every finding yourself.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        Four things are worth checking when you compare reports. Are the reproduction steps precise
        enough for your developer to follow? Is the fix specific to a stack, or is it "sanitise all
        input"? Does the impact section describe a business consequence or only a technical one? Is
        there an attack narrative showing how small findings combine?
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <ReportViewer />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CommandPalette />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-s);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
</style>
